{
  "Anything the user moves with the pointer, a finger or the arrow keys, along an axis or inside a boundary, by a handle or as a copy; and the targets that take it. For items that change places in a list, see [Sortable](/sortable).": "",
  "Moving things": "",
  "The JSX children are what moves. `boundary` keeps it inside its parent or an element, `axis` keeps it on a line, `handle` names the only part that takes the press and the keys. A drag writes the place to `x-model` and `onDragEnded` tells it; Escape brings it back.": "",
  "Drop targets": "",
  "A `DropTarget` of the same `group` takes a draggable dropped on it and is told in `onDropped` with the draggable’s `data`; `onDragEntering` may refuse. With `clone` a copy follows the pointer and the draggable stays, so one thing can be dropped many times. What a drop does to your data is yours.": "",
  "`position` puts it where you say, in pixels from where it was laid out, and `x-model` takes the place back after every drag or key: kept and restored.": "",
  "The draggable (or its handle) is one stop.": "",
  "Move it by `step` pixels along its axis, inside its boundary; the new place is read out.": "",
  "While dragging: lets go and brings it back where it started.": "",
  "A `group` with `aria-roledescription=\"draggable\"` named “Move” in the kit language; with a `handle`, that element is a button of that name instead.": "",
  "A long press lifts it on a touch screen. While it is dragged it lets the pointer through, so the target under it is found; the copy of a `clone` follows the pointer.": "",
  "Marked while a drag of their group is under way, while the draggable is over them, and when they refuse it.": "",
  "The draggable. `data-dragging`, `data-handle`, `data-clone`, `data-axis`.": "",
  "The handle named by `handle`; the copy after the pointer.": "",
  "A target. `data-drop-active` during a drag of its group, `data-drop-over`, `data-drop-refused`.": "",
  "Units: the draggable (`draggable`, `dragging`, `focus`), its handle (`hover`, `focus`), the copy.": "",
  "Unit: a target (`active`, `over`, `refused`).": "",
  "Draggable props": "",
  "`both`, `x` or `y`.": "",
  "The draggable stays inside this: its parent, or an element it lies in.": "",
  "A selector inside the draggable: only a press there drags it, and it takes the Tab stop and the keys.": "",
  "A copy follows the pointer and the draggable stays where it is; for a drop target to take.": "",
  "Drop targets of the same group take it.": "",
  "Anything of your own, given to the drop target with the drop.": "",
  "Pixels an arrow key moves it by.": "",
  "Where it stands, in pixels from where it was laid out: given, it is applied; after every drag or key the new place is written to `x-model`.": "",
  "DropTarget props and events": "",
  "Takes the draggables of this group; `null` takes those without one.": "",
  "A draggable came over it (`draggable`, `data`); `cancel = true` refuses it.": "",
  "The draggable left it.": "",
  "A draggable was dropped on it: your data is yours to move.": "",
  "A drag is about to begin; `cancel = true` keeps it in place.": "",
  "It is being dragged (`x`, `y`, the `target` under the pointer).": "",
  "The pointer let go; `cancel = true` brings it back where it started.": "",
  "The drag ended (`x`, `y`, `target`, `dropped`).": "",
  "Where it stands now.": "",
  "A drag is under way.": "",
  "What takes the press and the keys: the handle, else the draggable itself.": ""
}
